From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marlo <Plays.xenon@yahoo.de>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:21:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Editor M1 core: MapDocument, native command stack and commit
 path

MapDocument owns the height words; every edit is a Command (Do/Undo/Redo/TryMerge/Seal) on one stack. A brush stroke is
one command of sparse tile deltas, packed when the stroke ends, with before/after checksums so undo proves exactness.
History capped, dirty tracking follows a save point. The sink writes the view field at once and queues the rectangle;
Sim::AdvanceBeat applies the queue to the sim field and dirties the path clusters (no UI-thread writes to the sim field).
Natives ed_doc_* / ed_cmd_* (+ sim-state ed_sim_apply_pending / ed_sim_checksum); raw terrain natives go through the
document as external writes. Engine-free MapDocumentTest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

